# The version of every INDUSTRY MODULE this project's deployments install. THE SOURCE OF TRUTH (ADR 0799).
#
# A module used to be a bare DLL somebody copied into a directory. That is what #1242 cost: the kiosk served a
# build from four releases earlier, and establishing which one took comparing file mtimes and SHA-256 sums off
# the host, because nothing anywhere recorded it. A pinned package gives the four things a copied file cannot —
# a VERSION (an identity, not an mtime), a PIN per environment, a ROLLBACK (pin the previous version; today
# there is no "previous" to name), and PROVENANCE from the feed.
#
# This file is the sibling of images.env and follows its discipline: the value is named in more than one place,
# so the copies are CHECKED rather than trusted (ModulePinLockstepTests). It answers a different question,
# which is why it is a different file — images.env pins third-party services we RUN, this pins our own vertical
# software we INSTALL, and the two are consumed by different machinery.
#
# EACH ENTRY PINS A VERSION AND A DIGEST. GitHub Packages publishes a `.nupkg.sha512` beside every package, so
# the digest costs nothing to obtain, and verifying it before unpacking makes the installed bytes provable
# rather than assumed. A published NuGet version is already immutable, so this is belt-and-braces — carried
# anyway because "the bytes were not what anyone thought" has already happened once here.
#
# WHICH modules an environment installs is NOT decided here — that is `SA_MODULES` on the deployment (empty by
# default, so `docker compose up --build` needs no package credential and keeps working exactly as the README
# documents). This file only says WHICH VERSION, for every module any of our deployments knows how to install.
#
# TO BUMP: change both values for one module, then run the tests and fix exactly what they name.
# TO ROLL BACK: put the previous pair back. That is the whole procedure, and it is the point of the file.
#
# The digest is the BASE64 form NuGet publishes (the contents of `<id>.<version>.nupkg.sha512`), not hex —
# scripts/modules-init.sh compares against that form directly so the value can be copied from the feed verbatim.

# The flight-school vertical (its ADRs 0014–0019; core ADRs 0735–0744 and the ABI).
FLIGHT_SCHOOL_PACKAGE=SimplArchive.FlightSchool
FLIGHT_SCHOOL_VERSION=0.1.0
FLIGHT_SCHOOL_SHA512=lGAi9xuRaaMlOVag/9ggOEMFtlvGTRSOCnR0X0YbG54xZE1/dfbqONV6qp0kd3OShc0TnJzum7v3MyqG/qXaXw==

# ^ DELIBERATELY UNSET UNTIL THE MODULE REPO PUBLISHES ITS FIRST PACKAGE. The publishing half of ADR 0799 lives
# in the module's own repository, so there is no version to pin yet, and inventing one here would be a pin that
# names nothing. `SA_MODULES` is empty everywhere until then, so nothing resolves these — and the guard refuses
# a 0.0.0 pin the moment a deployment DOES ask for this module, rather than letting a placeholder ship.
